<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yekum_purkan/congregation"><tei:pb n="378" ed="1949 shabbat/shacharit/torah" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n402_medium.jpg"/><tei:p><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yekum_purkan/congregation/opening"/>May salvation arise from heaven. May grace, kindness and mercy—long life, ample sustenance and divine aid; physical health, perfect vision, and healthy children who will never neglect the study of the Torah—be granted <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yekum_purkan/congregation/text"/>to this entire congregation, great and small, women and children. May the King of the universe bless you, prolong your lives, increase your days and add to your years; may you be saved and delivered from all distress and disease. May our Lord who is in heaven be your help at all times; and let us say, Amen. <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p></tei:div>
